== overlaps qualification (per brief section 6 fallback): ==
- large prefill shapes (this run): measured overlap 5.03 ms per layer = 18.1% of layer kernel time (seq=256) and 1.28 ms = 11.2% (seq=32) — the double-buffered slot-B copy genuinely overlaps slot-A compute.
- small in-suite fixture (hidden 256, seq=6): microsecond-scale kernels; the first (cold) layer shows the initial slab-staging cost, the warm layer overlaps 0.06 ms (~42% of its tiny 0.145 ms kernel budget, ~60 microseconds absolute); NO meaningful throughput or overlap claim is made for such shapes.
- hipHostRegister never fired in these runs (synthetic tensor views are 32-byte aligned, not page aligned): the live pinned path is the per-slot pinned-slab fallback with a CPU memcpy that overlaps the previous kernel. No pageable-async claim is made.
